---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<SiteLayout
	title="About"
	description="About Tomorrow-ish, a clearly labeled satirical newspaper reporting tomorrow's headlines today."
	canonicalPath="/about"
>
	<header class="page-header">
		<p class="section-kicker">About the paper</p>
		<h1>Close enough to tomorrow.</h1>
	</header>

	<article class="prose-page">
		<p>
			Tomorrow-ish is a satirical newspaper that follows today’s events one questionable step into the future.
			Every headline and article on this site is fictional.
		</p>
		<h2>The premise</h2>
		<p>
			The news already contains the beginnings of its own absurd conclusions. Tomorrow-ish takes those beginnings
			seriously, extrapolates them irresponsibly, and publishes the result as tomorrow’s news today.
		</p>
		<h2>The standard</h2>
		<p>
			The aim is dry, intelligent satire presented with the care of a small newspaper—not fabricated reporting,
			misinformation, or a pile of memes wearing a trench coat.
		</p>
		<h2>The important part</h2>
		<p>
			Tomorrow-ish is satire. Do not rely on its fictional stories as factual reporting. Source and context links,
			when present, identify the real-world material that inspired a piece; they do not make the satire itself true.
		</p>
	</article>
</SiteLayout>
